From 67c6c9e95abc82740b53679c5abf4c230d5a763e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sneid1 <sneid1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:22:02 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] UYA sound: version 3 grains decoded, 989snd RNG from UYA's
 module image

SBlk version 3 grains (8-byte records: type << 24 | operand, delay) are translated at parse time to the
model's version 1 grains, with their operands read where UYA's 989snd grain handlers (table 0x1d638) read
them: tones and LFOs from the parameter area at SBlk +0x34, the rest from the three signed operand bytes.
The v3 loop end jumps back at most once per tick (flag 0x40), and type 44 (copy register) is new.

The driver's R250 table comes from UYA's 989snd module image in EE RAM at its init call: without it every
draw was 0, random waits never waited and looping ambiences took all 48 voices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oracle/src/rc3/hle.rs        | 16 +++++++
 oracle/src/snd989/bank.rs    | 93 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 oracle/src/snd989/handler.rs | 24 ++++++++--
 oracle/src/snd989/rng.rs     | 18 +++++++
 4 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

